From 5e59268cef7faddcf4ebee39c162e7d52197eb12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:23:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-PIP-001 wave 18e: video Picture-in-Picture for registry
 tabs

Route browser-less EnterPictureInPicture/ExitPictureInPicture to Chromium's PictureInPictureWindowManager and its Views overlay window once the host registers a PiP callback. ReArcTabSetPictureInPicture now enters through the tab's MediaSession (Chromium's own availability rule) and exits; media events carry real pip_available/pip_active. Entered/exited events and a back-to-tab focus request (only the activation that follows PiP's back-to-tab, never page window.focus()) reach the host. Without a callback page and host requests fail as before; Document PiP stays unsupported. ABI 1.30 / bridge 0.32.0; build p77, native refusal, page and host entry, host exit, back-to-tab and close while active pass.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
